# M39 (PLAN_BROWSER_PERF_SECURITY.md §2.10, D49) — isolated GET-only rung on the echo-server
# harness, split out of bench.tflw's combined GET+POST shape so this run's numbers reflect only
# the GET request, not an average across both steps. Zero-latency target (echo-server.mjs), same
# ramp shape as bench.tflw for consistency with the existing echo-server harness convention.

test "M39 echo GET-only"
  ramp to 30 users over 8s
  api GET /products
  expect status equals 200
